ind of like a mini study course  so  that leads us up to where we are now  it's early on enough in june that i can  i can really talk quite a bit about june  without having to do some backtracking  this is a month where i'll actually get  to take some vacation i'll get to go to  the beach for about a week with my my  wife and kids  we try to do that once a year  going going out to  montauk before the the season really  starts so the water is a little cold  but the beach isn't crowded and it's a  really nice way to relax for for us  um  and  what else have i got going on before  that there's the saint anselm  metaphysics colloquium up at st anselm  college i'll be going up there at that  one i don't have to talk although i will  of course talk because i always get  involved with chatting about things but  i don't have to do any presentations  they already have speakers for that and  i can just go and really just be a  student and and meet up with some old  friends  uh i've been going to saint anselm's  college since uh 2000 for for one  conference or another  now i'm up there about once or twice a  year  um what else is going on  i'm still in the process of building  more content for my existentialism class  that i'm i'm constructing for a plano  and i i've rethought some of the things  particularly for the early weeks how i  want the material to be lined up for  students i've said that a plareno puts  the instructor in the driver's seat as  far as the design of the class and that  can be a good thing but it can also be  you know something that leads to  things taking a bit longer if you if you  give it to somebody like me who's always  wanting to say well you know what if i  did this or what if i did that what if i  added this in what if i added that in  so  that should be coming out  i should be submitting it for for its  first review sometime this month  i'm also writing a  book chapter on on jacques laca and  ethics this month and i have just  finished with a  textbook proposal which i'm submitting  to to a textbook publisher  i had to write some some sample material  in this case the sample material was on  aristotle and happiness and the idea was  to write it in such a way that students  today can relate to it so i've drawn on  a lot of things from my my classes  um  i'll be doing another glimpses of  existence session  at the kingston public library at the  end of the month this time on the  russian philosopher lev shestoff a very  interesting existentialist  i'm doing in other theology matters  later this week on thursday night  and this one will be on the existence  and nature of god the way that augustine  understands these things which are you  know kind of interrelated with each  other  i'll be doing some more punk rock  philosopher segments some of which will  be on hegel's phenomenology some of  which we started getting into some  discussions about alexander kojov's  introduction to the reading of hegel  we're going to do another dr sailors  philosophy forum later this month but i  haven't decided  whether i want to do a guest or whether  i want to do one on my own  perhaps on existentialism  and i'm not sure exactly when i'm going  to do it it won't be it won't be this  coming weekend  uh and and so things are a little bit up  in the air for that so you know stay  stay tuned for that now videos we have a  lot of videos coming out this month more  half hour hegel  uh  more core concept videos these i'm  actually taking the opportunity to  produce more core concept videos for my  my own marist class students so some of  them are going to be on wd ross is the  right and the good  and his prima facie duties i did two of  them previously and i'd like to do the  other five some of them are on parts of  aristotle's nick and mccain ethics that  i hadn't gotten to before  like uh book five where he's talking  about about justice so i've done done  some core concept videos on that i'll do  another 10 shorts or maybe two this  month we'll see how many questions i get  and then i know i've been promising to  get to some existentialism videos but  it's been a matter of finding the time  but i'm ready to start shooting some on  kafka  and  perhaps even  we'll see how it goes for this month  perhaps even on dostoevsky's work the  demons or the possessed  so that's what we got going on uh  this coming month  you know i'm going to be taking a little  bit of down time  probably releasing some of the videos  during that time  and  enjoying my time with my my wife and  kids and while the weather is still you  know  mild before it becomes  unbearably hot and humid and i have to  dig out the air conditioner  so i hope that you'll watch some of  these  share some of the videos  tune in to the things that that interest  you maybe the theology matters or the  half the the um  punk rock philosopher if you're in the  area  and you're free  on on saturday uh mornings  then consider at the end of the month  popping in for my glimpses of existence  session on lev chest off  otherwise have a good month and uh  you'll see plenty of my face if you're  tuned in to my feed
 

